<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36645" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Plēĭŏnē</span></b> ,
			ēs, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πληϊόνη</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A daughter of Oceanus and Tethys</i>, <i>wife of Atlas and mother of the Pleiades</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hinc sata Pleione cum caelifero Atlante,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. F.
					5, 83</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Hyg. Astr. 2, 21</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pleiones nepos,</span>”
				i.e. <i>Mercury</i>, <i>son of Maia</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. H.
					16, 62</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Val.
				Fl. 1, 738</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>The constellation of the Pleiades</i>, <i><span class="en">Val. Fl. 2,
				67</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
